.TH TRAIL 1 "2026-08-18" "trail 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
trail \- read Ask session logs as JSONL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trail ls
.RI [ dir ]
.br
.B trail find
.I query
.RI [ dir ]
.br
.B trail show
.I session
.br
.B trail window
.RB [ \-before " " n ]
.RB [ \-after " " n ]
.I session seq
.br
.B trail lineage
.I session
.RI [ dir ]
.br
.B trail check
.RI [ dir ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B trail
is a read-only browser for Ask session archives.
It writes one JSON object per line to standard output.
It never writes or repairs a session and never maintains an index.
.PP
A session argument is an existing path, or otherwise a bare id resolved in
the default archive directory.
Archive commands scan regular files ending in
.B .jsonl
in lexical path order.
They ignore directories and symbolic links.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ls
Write one
.B session
summary per file.
.TP
.B find
Write one
.B match
record per matching event.
Matching is a literal substring search after Unicode case folding and
whitespace collapse.
The printed text is unchanged.
.TP
.B show
Write every valid archived event inside an
.B event
record.
Unknown event types and fields are preserved.
.TP
.B window
Write the event at
.I seq
and neighboring events.
The default is three events before and after.
.TP
.B lineage
Write
.B node
and
.B edge
records for the connected component containing the session.
Only parent and summary ids recorded by Ask are edges.
Trail does not infer ancestry from copied files.
.TP
.B check
Run
.B ask replay \-check FILE
for every archive file and write a
.B check
record for each verdict.
.TP
.B version
Print the Trail version.
.TP
.B help
Print a command summary.
.SH OUTPUT
Standard output is JSONL.
Record kinds are
.BR session ,
.BR match ,
.BR event ,
.BR node ,
.BR edge ,
.BR check ,
.BR warning ,
and
.BR error .
Fatal diagnostics go to standard error.
.PP
Damage in one file produces an error record and does not prevent later files
from being read.
An invalid final record produces a warning and is ignored in memory as a torn
append; the file is not changed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ASK_DIR
Default archive and bare-id directory.
If unset, the default is
.BR ~/.ask/sessions .
.TP
.B ASK
Ask executable used only by
.BR check .
The default is
.B ask
on
.BR PATH .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful result.
.TP
.B 1
No search match, missing sequence, archive damage, or failed replay check.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage or operating error.
.SH SEARCH FIELDS
Find searches user and assistant text, reasoning, attachment names and media
types, notes, retry and terminal errors, and request model and effort labels.
It excludes system prompts, base64 media, provider-native state, digests,
schemas, and fields in unknown event types.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ask (1),
.BR jq (1)
